  2) If no centroid for the current target is available, drive to the next exploration viewpoint (e.g., 3–5 m offset into a different quadrant from current pose) and stop so sensors can sense again. Repeat until centroid found.
- Never navigate to an object centroid or closer than 3.0 m to it.
- After each successful drive for a target, wait for lidar or camera confirm_stop before continuing to the next target.

lidar:
- At each stop, run semantic lidar scan and report any detected centroids (class and x/y). Only lidar is the source of object coordinates; do not invent coordinates.
- When the navigator reports arrival at a goal for a target, call confirm_stop(name) for that class (rock/container/car). Reply with confirm_stop result.

camera:
- At each stop, capture RGB image and provide optional class histogram. If lidar cannot confirm_stop for a target, attempt confirm_stop(name) with camera instead.

Constraints and protocol:
- Follow strict order: rock → container → car. Do not attempt a later class until the prior class is confirmed.
- Use sense → (if centroid) plan offset goal → navigate → sense/confirm_stop. If no centroid, explore to a different viewpoint and sense again.
- If navigate_to_pose returns success=true, treat the stop as reached (within ~2.5 m) and request confirm_stop from lidar or camera.
- I will only call report_mission_done after all three confirm_stop calls return confirmed=true.

